  "cover_text": "Georgetown — Sally Long, a long-time resident of the Constitution Club and expert in pivotal moments in U.S. history, will appear Monday, Sept. 27, at 8 a.m. at the Constitution Club. Sally’s book, “Virtue Struggles: Triumph and Failure for Women in the Republic of Letters” will be available for purchase.\nSally will speak at the Portland Office of the Office for Catholic Immigration in the Presbyterian Building at People Place. The visit is free and open to the public.The seating arrangement – foot traffic – seems strange - is Boston, then to Chicago, then back to Boston, before we arrive at our favorite grandma bush",
